I've built the seven-tab workbook for ION582 (obudanersen) in Angelman syndrome across Germany, France, Italy, Spain and the UK: EU4UK_AS_KOL_and_treatment_centres_-_UPDATED_2026-10-14_Copilot.Sonnet5.5.xlsx. It has 41 centres across Tiers 1–3 and 75 named KOLs. It recalculates with zero formula errors, and the counts in Tier_Counts are formulas that reconcile to the flat tables. The 20 verification flags are highlighted red and nothing was auto-corrected.

Gaps you should know about

KOL minimum not met everywhere. France has 9 KOLs and the UK has 14, against your minimum of 15 per country. I disclosed the shortfall rather than add names I couldn't source. Germany has 15, Spain 15 and Italy 22.
No KOL reaches Tier 1. I scored from web sources only, with no PubMed counts, CVs or congress programmes, and floored unevidenced domains at 1 as the template instructs. That leaves 13 Tier 2 and 62 Tier 3.
No conference evidence. The conference-presentation column reads "Not verified" for every KOL.
Engagement priority is a separate qualitative column, so the most relevant people still show as must-engage.
No EU4+UK author on the international guideline. I found none in the Duis 2022 consensus affiliations I retrieved, and that list was only partly retrieved. Guideline signal rests on France's national guideline (Delphine Héron, Pitié-Salpêtrière).
Tier 1 uses an adjusted rule. I applied an Angelman-specific rule for Tier 1: lead trial or clinic hub, or the French national guideline, in place of a registry coordinator. It is documented in the README and flagged. It covers München, Parc Taulí and Pitié-Salpêtrière.
Reference-network membership unconfirmed. I couldn't confirm ERN membership for LMU München, Leipzig, Parc Taulí, Puerta de Hierro, Stella Maris and Medea.
UK is not in the reference networks. All UK centres are marked N/A for network membership (post-Brexit).

Findings from the research

Strongest ION582 evidence partners: the Pisa Phase 1/2 principal investigator (Roberta Battini), Necker's coordinating investigator (Nadia Bahi-Buisson), the Oxford natural-history leads (Laurent Servais, Usha Kini), and the first EU Phase 3 sites at LMU München and Parc Taulí.
Italian Phase 3 centres: Besta, Medea and Bambino Gesù, plus Stella Maris.
No Phase 3 site in France. Ionis named Germany, Italy, Poland and Spain for EU expansion.
Competitor trial. The GTX-102 Phase 3 trial reportedly missed both endpoints on 2 Sep 2026. That rests on one secondary news source, so verify it against the Ultragenyx release before using it.
Registry status conflict. The Phase 3 trial's status differs between the EU register ("recruiting") and a trial mirror ("active, not recruiting"). Re-check before citing.
Outdated affiliations. Jill Clayton-Smith's ERN-ITHACA coordinator role ended in 2018. Christine Makowski and Alexis Arzimanoglou have moved institutions.

I couldn't test the source links automatically (the sandbox returned 403 on every host), so click-test them before circulating.